      'each gps satellite continuously broadcasts a signal that says exactly where the satellite is and exactly what time it is by a very precise atomic clock the receiver compares the incoming code with its own copy to measure how long the signal took to arrive and multiplies by the speed of light to get its distance to that satellite a pseudorange',
